# CODEOWNERS
# Each line is a file pattern followed by one or more owners.
#
# Policy: the fleet publisher merges routine PRs (dependency bumps, i18n,
# docs, app-code features) unattended once required status checks are
# green. Only paths listed below require human code-owner review before
# merge — everything else is intentionally left uncovered so it keeps
# auto-merging. This file is scoped to genuinely sensitive surfaces:
# crypto, wire format, the PSTN/notification sidecars that handle caller
# and volunteer identifiers, CI/supply-chain, release manifests,
# deployment config, the guard config that constrains agents, and the
# security-relevant test suites. There is no catch-all `*` rule — do not
# add one without re-evaluating this policy, since it would gate every
# PR again.
#
# Consequence worth calling out: GitHub Actions dependency bumps (e.g.
# Dependabot PRs touching .github/workflows/) now require review, because
# a compromised or malicious action is a supply-chain vector.

packages/crypto/                    @rhonda-rodododo
packages/protocol/schemas/          @rhonda-rodododo

# Deanonymization surfaces: sip-bridge/ routes PSTN calls and handles
# caller phone numbers; signal-notifier/ does HMAC-hashed contact
# resolution. Both are top-level, NOT under apps/ despite what older
# docs say.
sip-bridge/                         @rhonda-rodododo
signal-notifier/                    @rhonda-rodododo

.github/workflows/                  @rhonda-rodododo

knope.toml                          @rhonda-rodododo

CODEOWNERS                          @rhonda-rodododo
.claude/settings.json               @rhonda-rodododo

deploy/                             @rhonda-rodododo

tests/                              @rhonda-rodododo
packages/test-specs/                @rhonda-rodododo
apps/worker/__tests__/              @rhonda-rodododo
